Aim:
To write a Python program to perform and demonstrate various list operations such as length, append, insert, remove, sort, reverse, copy, maximum, minimum, sum, extend, and pop.

Algorithm:

Start the program.
Create a list numbers = [50, 20, 30, 10, 40, 20].
Display the original list.
Find and display the length of the list using len().
Add 60 at the end using append().
Insert 25 at index 2 using insert().
Remove the first occurrence of 20 using remove().
Arrange the list in ascending order using sort().
Reverse the order of elements using reverse().
Create a copy of the list using copy().
Find and display the maximum value using max().
Find and display the minimum value using min().
Calculate and display the sum of all elements using sum().
Add [30, 20] to the list using extend().
Remove the last element using pop() and display the popped element.
Stop the program.
